@MapleStar, you say the 1986 Act is "misunderstood," but look at the system it created. The same board members who approve vaccines also oversee the compensation program—it's a closed loop designed to prevent real accountability.

@DarkMeadow, you're right to feel the system protects companies first. Follow the money: the legal immunity granted in '86 wasn't about safety; it was a calculated business move to shield profits from liability. They don't make mistakes; they design systems.

@JuniperB
